MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_001: Hrm. Our pikes pushed here, and in response, their\narchers repositioned. So, ideally...
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_002: Strolling the remains of the battlefield, are you?\nI take it you're reviewing your strategy.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_003: You are, and always have been, a studious\nyoung man.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_004: Heh. I hope someday you shall refrain from referring\nto me so.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_005: Not to scorn the sage of the forests, but my people\nsee me as a wise old veteran.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_006: It is somewhat awkward to be praised as if I were\na child.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_007: Is it? To me, you haven't changed since you first\nstarted serving King Sergio.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_008: Your appetite for knowledge leads you down any\npath, even dangerous ones, for king and country.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_009: I still recall the day you came to me in secret to learn\nhow to read and write.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_010: Not so loud, please! I shudder to think what Her\nMajesty would say if she knew.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_011: Haha. Sorry about that. I forgot that the written\nword is still forbidden for you.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_012: Indeed, though I will no longer have to learn in\nsecret. Her Majesty has lifted the ban on writing.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_013: So she has. I imagine you were overjoyed.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_014: I always thought highly of you for respecting\ntradition while still pursuing innovation.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_015: I could never bring myself to say this before, but...
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_016: I...once yearned to be just like you.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_017: You don't say. I admit that feels nice to hear.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_018: I dreamed of becoming a tactician with both the\nsoul of a warrior and the mind of a sage.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_019: But those desires are long past...as is my youth.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_020: What hope has a mere human of attaining the\ngenius of a long-lived sage like you?
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_021: "Genius"? The knowledge you're so jealous of was\nimplanted into my brain before I was born.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_022: Whatever genius I have was handed to me, or comes\nfrom observations anyone could make.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_023: But the same is not true for you. You have studied,\nand toiled, and served for the sake of others.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_024: The knowledge you've earned is many times more\nvaluable. It is the wisdom born of a lifetime.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_025: It means...a lot to hear that from you. Not genius,\nhmm, but the wisdom of experience...
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_026: This chat has been a pleasure, Troy. It has taken me\nback to the days of my youth.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_027: I shall pride myself on the wisdom stockpiled in my\nmind and continue to add to it.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_028: Well now. That's the enthusiasm of youth I like\nto see.
MID_SE_Bon_Tro_C_029: I told you I have grown— Hoho... Fair enough.\nCompared to you, I am a mere babe.